1
00:00:00,152 --> 00:00:02,152
We might consider Schrödinger's cat.

2
00:00:02,821 --> 00:00:05,411
Schrödinger. Is that the woman in 2A?

3
00:00:05,574 --> 00:00:06,824
(Sheldon:)No, that's Mrs. Grossinger.

4
00:00:06,992 --> 00:00:10,492
(Sheldon:)She doesn't have a cat, she has a Mexican
hairless. Annoying little animal. Yip-yip-yip.

5
00:00:10,662 --> 00:00:12,162
(Sheldon:)Sheldon.

6
00:00:13,415 --> 00:00:14,665
(Sheldon:)Sorry, you diverted me.

7
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:19,253
Anyway, in 1935, Erwin Schrödinger,
in an attempt to explain...

8
00:00:19,421 --> 00:00:23,091
(Sheldon:)...the Copenhagen interpretation of quantum
physics, he proposed an experiment.

9
00:00:23,258 --> 00:00:26,888
(Sheldon:)A cat is placed in a box
with a sealed vial of poison...

10
00:00:27,054 --> 00:00:28,974
(Sheldon:)...that will break open at a random time.

11
00:00:29,139 --> 00:00:32,939
Now, since no one knows
when or if the poison has been released...

12
00:00:33,101 --> 00:00:38,611
(Sheldon:)...until the box is opened, the cat
can be thought of as both alive and dead.

13
00:00:43,654 --> 00:00:45,194
(Penny:)I'm sorry, I don't get the point.

14
00:00:45,364 --> 00:00:48,404
(Sheldon:)Well, of course you don't get it.
I haven't made it yet.

15
00:00:49,993 --> 00:00:52,163
You have to be psychic,
there's no such thing...

16
00:00:52,329 --> 00:00:53,869
(Penny:)Sheldon, what's the point?

17
00:00:54,039 --> 00:00:57,709
Just like Schrödinger's cat,
your potential relationship with Leonard...

18
00:00:57,876 --> 00:01:00,546
(Howard:)...right now
can be thought of as both good and bad.

